Z16-P01 | Emergency Scene Safety and STOP Triad Cross-Reference | New manuscript (Z16 P20 emergency index)
objective: Index immediate scene-safety, lost-person STOP, and 911 escalation gates across Z01, Z10, and Z11 without dropping upstream limits.
applies: First 60 seconds of any backcountry, weather, or trauma emergency.
equipment: Full offline reader (Z01, Z10, Z11), primary zone cards, and local emergency and agency references.
diagram: Locate Z01, Z10, Z11 cards | Preserve exact stop & limits | Defer to full zone card
visual: Cross-zone atlas schematic linking Z01, Z10, Z11 with preserved upstream conditions and stop thresholds.
action: Pause on stable ground (Z01-P01, Z11-P43) to scan active traffic, water, ice, fire, electrical, or overhead-snag hazards before approaching a casualty or moving further. @A01,T01
action: Activate 911 or emergency SOS early (Z01-P16, Z10-P01) while establishing shelter, bleeding control, or rescue signaling rather than delaying for uncertain self-rescue. @A01,A09,M01
action: Defer immediately to the full upstream Z01, Z10, or Z11 card for scene-specific exclusions; never treat a condensed atlas summary as standalone clinical clearance. @A01,A10
failure: Rushing into an active water, ice, gas, electrical, or wildlife hazard creates a second casualty and delays rescue. @A01,T01
verify: Scene hazards are checked, exact upstream Z01, Z10, Z11 card IDs are located, and emergency help is notified early. @A01,A09
stop: Stop advancing into any unverified hazard zone and hold on safe ground until qualified responders or verified conditions permit movement. @A01,T01
reviewer: SAR, EMS, and emergency-management reviewer

Z16-P02 | Life-Threatening Bleeding and Civilian Tourniquet Cross-Reference | New manuscript (Z16 P20 emergency index)
objective: Cross-reference Z10 hemorrhage control, Z09 sharp-tool laceration risks, and Z06 field-trauma readiness while preserving civilian visible-wound tourniquet rules.
applies: Severe arterial, venous bleeding from falls, tools, siliceous stone, or hunting incidents.
equipment: Full offline reader (Z10, Z06, Z09), primary zone cards, and local emergency and agency references.
diagram: Locate Z10, Z06, Z09 cards | Preserve exact stop & limits | Defer to full zone card
visual: Cross-zone atlas schematic linking Z10, Z06, Z09 with preserved upstream conditions and stop thresholds.
action: Apply firm continuous direct pressure on visible life-threatening bleeding and pack junctional wounds per Z10-P03 and Z10-P04 while activating 911 immediately. @A01,M01
action: For visible life-threatening extremity hemorrhage, apply a commercial windlass tourniquet 2 to 3 inches above the wound—never over a joint—tightening until bleeding stops and recording application time (Z10-P04); separate tactical high-and-tight contexts and pediatric fit limits remain binding. @A01,M02
action: Secure tools, knives, saws, or unloaded firearms (Z06-P48, Z09-P02) away from casualties and monitor continuously for shock (Z10-P05) without giving oral fluids to impaired patients. @A01,M05,H03
failure: Mixing tactical high-and-tight instructions with visible-wound spacing, loosening a needed tourniquet, or using improvised narrow cords causes fatal blood loss. @M01,M02
verify: Direct pressure or properly placed commercial tourniquet stops bright bleeding, time is noted, and 911 is en route. @M01,M02
stop: Stop improvised tourniquet experiments when commercial gear or firm direct pressure, packing is indicated, and never remove a placed tourniquet outside clinician direction. @M01,M02
reviewer: Trauma EMS and wilderness-medicine reviewer

Z16-P03 | Airway, CPR, Choking and Drowning Resuscitation Cross-Reference | New manuscript (Z16 P20 emergency index)
objective: Index adult, pediatric, and drowning resuscitation distinctions across Z10 and Z12 without stripping dispatcher guidance or rescue-breath exceptions.
applies: Unresponsive casualty, choking, or post-immersion drowning rescue.
