visual: Cross-zone atlas schematic linking Z10, Z12, Z06 with preserved upstream conditions and stop thresholds.
action: Check responsiveness and normal breathing rapidly without imposing an arbitrary full-minute delay, activate 911, AED immediately, and follow dispatcher-guided CPR (Z10-P08, Z10-P09). @A01,M03
action: Preserve Z10 and Z12 cause-specific distinctions: drowning and pediatric cardiac arrest prioritize rescue breaths alongside compressions when trained, rather than assuming hands-only CPR fits every casualty. @A01,M03,X03
action: In water or ice incidents (Z12-P16, Z06-P20), enforce Reach-Throw-Dont-Go shore-based assistance so untrained rescuers do not enter cold water and drown. @A01,X03,H18
failure: Delaying compressions for prolonged checks, omitting rescue breaths in drowning, pediatric arrest, or swimming after victims causes preventable fatalities. @M03,X03
verify: 911 and AED are activated immediately, dispatcher instructions are followed, and shore-rescue limits hold. @M03,X03
stop: Stop hands-only assumptions for drowning or pediatric patients when trained for breaths, and never enter unstable ice or surf without rescue gear. @M03,X03
reviewer: EMS, resuscitation, and water-rescue reviewer

Z16-P04 | Carbon Monoxide Immediate Evacuation and Combustion Clearance Index | New manuscript (Z16 P20 emergency index)
objective: Consolidate zero-delay CO alarm evacuation and outdoor-only combustion boundaries across Z02, Z03, Z13, and Z15.
applies: Any tent, cabin, vehicle, basement, or home using stoves, heaters, fireplaces, or portable generators.
equipment: Full offline reader (Z02, Z03, Z13, Z15), primary zone cards, and local emergency and agency references.
diagram: Locate Z02, Z03, Z13, Z15 cards | Preserve exact stop & limits | Defer to full zone card
visual: Cross-zone atlas schematic linking Z02, Z03, Z13, Z15 with preserved upstream conditions and stop thresholds.
action: Evacuate everyone immediately into fresh outdoor air and call 911 or the fire department whenever a CO alarm sounds or CO symptoms appear (Z13-P20, Z03-P40)—never delay exit to shut down equipment. @A01,C07,U05
action: Operate portable generators strictly outdoors at least 20 feet from windows, doors, vents, and garages with exhaust pointed away (Z03-P06, Z13-P06), and never run fuel stoves, grills, or charcoal inside tents, snow caves, vehicles, or enclosures (Z02-P44). @A01,C05,C06,U04
action: Clear snow-buried furnace, dryer exterior PVC vents (Z13-P24) and stranded-vehicle tailpipes (Z15-P14) before operating heating appliances or engines. @A01,U07,D19
failure: Stopping to turn off a generator or furnace during a CO alarm—or cracking a tent zipper while burning a stove—causes fatal hypoxic collapse. @C05,C07,U05
verify: Battery-backed CO alarms are installed, generators sit at least 20 ft outdoors, and immediate fresh-air exit precedes any equipment action. @C06,C07,U04,U05
stop: Stop all indoor fuel combustion immediately and leave the building at once on any CO alarm or unexplained headache, dizziness. @C07,U05
reviewer: Fire service, HVAC/CO, and wilderness-shelter reviewer

Z16-P05 | Hypothermia, Cold-Water Shock and Frostbite Cross-Reference | New manuscript (Z16 P20 emergency index)
objective: Integrate cold-exposure prevention, hypothermia gentle handling, and non-refreezing frostbite rules across Z02, Z10, Z12, and Z13.
applies: Cold rain, wind chill, winter outages, snow travel, and cold-water immersion.
equipment: Full offline reader (Z02, Z10, Z12, Z13), primary zone cards, and local emergency and agency references.
diagram: Locate Z02, Z10, Z12, Z13 cards | Preserve exact stop & limits | Defer to full zone card
visual: Cross-zone atlas schematic linking Z02, Z10, Z12, Z13 with preserved upstream conditions and stop thresholds.
action: Prioritize dry ground insulation, windproof shelter, and vapor, moisture control (Z02-P03, Z12-P04) before cold stress advances to shivering cessation or confusion. @A01,E03,X02
action: Handle severe hypothermia gently, insulate from ground, avoid rapid peripheral rubbing or alcohol, and activate EMS early (Z10-P42, Z12-P08); for frostbite, never rub with snow or thaw tissue if refreezing is possible (Z10-P44). @A01,M11,M12,X02
action: During winter power outages (Z13-P18, Z15-P13), consolidate into one safe insulated interior room or move early to a designated public warming center rather than using unsafe unvented heaters. @A01,U06,D19
failure: Rubbing frostbitten digits with snow, thawing feet before a cold hike out, or rough handling of severely hypothermic patients worsens tissue loss and cardiac arrhythmia. @M11,M12
verify: Dry ground barrier, gentle warming, non-refreezing frostbite rule, and warming-center, EMS triggers are preserved intact. @E03,M11,M12
stop: Stop outdoor travel and activate rescue immediately when shivering stops, speech slurs, or coordination fails. @M11,X02
reviewer: Wilderness medicine and cold-weather rescue reviewer

Z16-P06 | Extreme Heat Stroke Cooling and Indoor Fan Limit Cross-Reference | New manuscript (Z16 P20 emergency index)
objective: Align rapid heat-stroke cooling, CDC indoor fan limits, and desert, urban heat triggers across Z10, Z12, and Z15.
applies: Summer heat waves, power outages with high indoor heat, and desert or heavy-exertion travel.
equipment: Full offline reader (Z10, Z12, Z15), primary zone cards, and local emergency and agency references.
diagram: Locate Z10, Z12, Z15 cards | Preserve exact stop & limits | Defer to full zone card
