action: Recognize heat stroke (confusion, altered alertness, collapse, very high body heat) as a life-threatening emergency requiring immediate 911 activation AND rapid cooling simultaneously (Z10-P46, Z12-P30). @A01,M27,X07
action: Use cold-water immersion when safely accessible and airway-protected, or continuous water dousing plus brisk airflow, and never force oral fluids into a confused or vomiting patient (Z10-P46). @A01,M27
action: Apply CDC indoor heat guidance in Z15-P37: indoor electric fans are advised only below 90 F; move to a cooler air-conditioned shelter or cooling center when indoor temperatures climb above safe limits. @A01,D21
failure: Delaying active cooling while awaiting EMS, giving fluids to altered patients, or relying solely on fans in >90 F rooms causes fatal organ failure. @M27,D21
verify: 911 + immediate cooling, airway fluid exclusion, and CDC below 90 F fan boundaries stay harmonized across zones. @M27,D21
stop: Stop exertion immediately on dizziness, nausea, or confusion and initiate aggressive cooling plus 911. @M27,X07
reviewer: Emergency medicine and public-health heat reviewer

Z16-P07 | Water Treatment, Altitude Boiling and Chemical Rejection Cross-Reference | New manuscript (Z16 P20 emergency index)
objective: Synthesize Z04 microbial treatment, altitude boiling duration, HAB, chemical source rejection, and Z13 boil-water, private-well rules.
applies: Backcountry water sourcing, flood boil-water advisories, and household emergency storage.
equipment: Full offline reader (Z04, Z12, Z13), primary zone cards, and local emergency and agency references.
diagram: Locate Z04, Z12, Z13 cards | Preserve exact stop & limits | Defer to full zone card
visual: Cross-zone atlas schematic linking Z04, Z12, Z13 with preserved upstream conditions and stop thresholds.
action: Separate visual clarification (settling, cloth strain) from validated microbial treatment; clear water is NEVER proven potable by appearance alone (Z04-P01, Z04-P32). @A03,W01,W03
action: Preserve exact CDC boiling conditions: bring water to a rolling boil for 1 full minute below 6,500 feet elevation and 3 full minutes above 6,500 feet (Z04-P34); pair filtration with viral disinfection or boiling where viruses exist (Z04-P37). @A03,W11,W15
action: Reject chemical spills, industrial, mine runoff, and cyanobacterial harmful algal blooms (HABs) outright—boiling concentrates cyanotoxins and does not remove lead, nitrates, or fuels (Z04-P14, Z13-P41). @A03,W04,W05,U11
failure: Omission of the 6,500-ft boiling altitude rule or boiling HAB, chemically polluted water causes severe illness or toxin concentration. @W04,W05,W11
verify: Clarification, elevation-adjusted boiling, filter freeze-damage checks, and chemical, HAB exclusions remain intact. @W04,W11,W15
stop: Stop using any water source suspected of chemical spills, fuel sheen, mine runoff, or algal blooms; use stored bottled water or relocate. @W04,W05
reviewer: Drinking-water microbiology and public-health reviewer

Z16-P08 | Plant, Berry and Wild Mushroom Poison Emergency Cross-Reference | New manuscript (Z16 P20 emergency index)
objective: Link Z05 lethal lookalikes, Z10 toxicology first response, and Z14 botulism red flags to immediate 1-800-222-1222 and 911 escalation.
applies: Any suspected ingestion of unknown plants, berries, roots, wild mushrooms, or suspect home-canned foods.
equipment: Full offline reader (Z05, Z10, Z14), primary zone cards, and local emergency and agency references.
diagram: Locate Z05, Z10, Z14 cards | Preserve exact stop & limits | Defer to full zone card
visual: Cross-zone atlas schematic linking Z05, Z10, Z14 with preserved upstream conditions and stop thresholds.
action: Call 911 immediately for airway swelling, breathing difficulty, seizures, confusion, vision, swallowing trouble, or collapse; call Poison Help (1-800-222-1222) at once for ANY suspected plant or mushroom ingestion without waiting for symptoms (Z05-P135, Z10-P61). @A09,B09,M19
action: Preserve delayed-onset red alerts: 6–24 hour GI onset with a deceptive day-two lull signals potentially fatal amatoxin poisoning (Amanita, Galerina, Z05-P133), while blurred vision, slurred speech, or swallowing trouble after preserved foods signals botulism emergency (Z14-P61). @A03,B06,P23
action: Save uneaten plant or mushroom pieces in dry paper bags (never sealed plastic, Z05-P134) and never induce vomiting uninstructed or open suspect bulging canning jars (Z14-P62). @A09,B08,P23
failure: Waiting for symptoms to worsen, sealing mushrooms in plastic, or tasting suspect canned food leads to preventable organ failure or respiratory paralysis. @B06,B08,P23
verify: 911 vs 1-800-222-1222 pathways, dry-paper specimen retention, and zero uninstructed emetics are preserved intact. @B08,B09,P23
stop: Stop all field activity and seek emergency clinical evaluation immediately after any suspected toxic plant, mushroom, or botulism exposure. @B09,P23
reviewer: Clinical medical toxicologist and mycologist

Z16-P09 | Severe Weather Immediate Action: Tornado, Flood and Lightning Index | New manuscript (Z16 P20 emergency index)
objective: Synthesize NWS immediate protective actions for tornadoes, flash floods, and lightning across Z11, Z12, and Z15 without losing exceptions.
applies: Active NWS Tornado Warning, Flash Flood Warning, Severe Thunderstorm, or visible lightning.
equipment: Full offline reader (Z11, Z12, Z15), primary zone cards, and local emergency and agency references.
diagram: Locate Z11, Z12, Z15 cards | Preserve exact stop & limits | Defer to full zone card
visual: Cross-zone atlas schematic linking Z11, Z12, Z15 with preserved upstream conditions and stop thresholds.
action: For tornadoes (Z15-P16..P18), move to a basement, safe room, or lowest interior windowless room—NEVER shelter under a highway overpass or remain in a mobile home. @A01,D04,D05
action: For flooding (Z15-P24..P26), obey Turn Around Dont Drown—NEVER drive or walk across flooded roads or around barricades; move to higher ground immediately. @A01,D07
action: For lightning (Z11-P38, Z12-P38, Z10-P50), leave open water, ridgelines, and isolated trees early for a substantial building or hard-topped vehicle; lightning victims retain no electrical charge and require immediate 911 and safe CPR if unresponsive. @A01,N05,M28
failure: Sheltering under highway overpasses, driving into murky floodwater over washed-out culverts, or hesitating to touch a lightning casualty causes fatalities. @D04,D07,M28
verify: Local NWS warning tiers, zero overpass, flood-crossing prohibitions, and lightning-casualty safety remain aligned. @D04,D07,M28
stop: Stop outdoor travel immediately upon NWS warnings, approaching thunder, or rising water over roadways. @D04,D07,N05
reviewer: Meteorologist and emergency-management reviewer

Z16-P10 | Compound Hazard Tradeoffs: Smoke+Heat, Outage+Cold and Flood+Power | New manuscript (Z16 P20 compound hazards)
objective: Preserve A02 compound-hazard boundaries where single-hazard instructions conflict (wildfire smoke plus heat, outage plus subzero cold, flood plus wet electrical panels).
applies: Multi-hazard events requiring simultaneous protection from conflicting environmental threats.
