action: When wildfire smoke coincides with extreme indoor heat or cooling failure (Z15-P33, Z15-P37), do not trap occupants in an overheated uncooled room—relocate to a cooler cleaner-air public shelter per EPA, local guidance. @A08,D20,D21
action: When flooding enters a basement or structure (Z13-P45, Z15-P28), stay strictly clear of standing water near electrical panels, outlets, or submerged tools and require licensed electrician, utility clearance before restoring power. @A08,U20
action: When extended winter power outages coincide with subzero cold (Z13-P18, Z15-P13), prioritize safe indoor heat consolidation or early relocation to a warming center while maintaining zero-delay CO evacuation. @A08,U05,D19
failure: Applying one single-hazard checklist blindly—such as sealing windows tightly during dangerous indoor heat or wading into a flooded basement to flip breakers—creates fatal secondary hazards. @D20,U20
verify: Compound-hazard conflict rules defer cleanly to local emergency-management orders and preserve every upstream stop condition. @A08,D20,U20
stop: Stop sheltering in place whenever indoor temperatures, smoke infiltration, floodwater, or CO alarms make the structure unsafe; evacuate per local authority. @A08,D20,U20
reviewer: Emergency management, public health, and licensed electrical reviewer

