Z16-P14 | Ice Safety, Deterioration and Zero-Guarantee Cross-Reference | New manuscript (Z16 P20 seasonal index)
objective: Harmonize Minnesota DNR ice-thickness guidance, spring candled-ice hazards, and B013 zero-guarantee angling boundaries across Z06, Z11, and Z12.
applies: Early freeze-up, mid-winter snow-insulated ice, and spring thaw on lakes and rivers.
equipment: Full offline reader (Z06, Z11, Z12), primary zone cards, and local emergency and agency references.
diagram: Locate Z06, Z11, Z12 cards | Preserve exact stop & limits | Defer to full zone card
visual: Cross-zone atlas schematic linking Z06, Z11, Z12 with preserved upstream conditions and stop thresholds.
action: Enforce the universal Z12, B013 rule: NO ice is ever 100% safe, prior foot or vehicle tracks never certify ice strength, and Minnesota DNR thickness guidelines apply only to new, clear, solid ice (Z12-P13, Z06-P01). @A02,X03,H18
action: Keep angling strictly secondary to survival priorities—never improvise ice holes without proper tools, flotation, rescue picks, and verified thickness measurements (Z06-P01, Z06-P02). @A02,H18,X03
action: Avoid river inlets, outlets, springs, pressure ridges, beaver runs, and spring candled vertical-column ice unconditionally, using Reach-Throw-Dont-Go shore assistance for any immersion emergency (Z12-P16, Z07-P25). @A02,X03,L13
failure: Trusting a single shoreline measurement or stepping onto snow-covered spring ice triggers sudden cold-water shock and drowning. @X03,H18
verify: Zero-guarantee ice rules, current, inlet exclusions, flotation wear, and shore-only rescue boundaries remain aligned. @X03,H18
stop: Stop at the shoreline whenever ice thickness, clarity, current influence, or rescue gear is uncertain. @X03,H18
reviewer: Ice-rescue and DNR safety reviewer

