action: Check outdoor fire restrictions before lighting any open flame (Z03-P37) and carry redundant waterproof ignition (lighters, storm matches, ferrocerium rod) paired with dry tinder while keeping a no-fire emergency fallback (Z03-P03, Z03-P19, Z03-P42). @A01,C01,C03,C16
action: Prevent canister-stove overheating explosions: NEVER wrap a full enclosing windscreen tightly around an upright isobutane canister stove (Z03-P28); switch to inverted-canister or cold-rated liquid-fuel stoves in sub-freezing temperatures (Z03-P25, Z12-P06). @A01,C12,C15
action: Refuel liquid-fuel and alcohol stoves strictly outdoors after flames are completely extinguished and metal is cool (Z03-P29), never priming or cooking inside tents, vestibules, or enclosed rooms (Z03-P40). @A01,C05,C12
failure: Wrapping an upright fuel canister tightly, pouring alcohol into a hot burner with invisible flame, or firing stoves inside vestibules causes flash burns, explosions, and CO death. @C05,C12
verify: Outdoor level mineral-soil setup, open canister airflow, cool refueling, and complete cold-out extinguishment are confirmed. @C01,C05,C12
stop: Stop using any stove showing fuel leaks, erratic yellow flaring, or hot canister walls; let cool completely and switch to no-fire plans. @C12,C16
reviewer: Appliance-safety and fire-prevention reviewer

