action: Enforce strict blade, saw exclusion zones (blood circle, kneeling or stable bracing, zero cutting toward thighs, hands, Z09-P02..P04) and reject storm blowdowns, hung-up snags, and tensioned spring poles unless trained with full sawyer PPE (Z09-P25, Z09-P26). @A04,K08,K10
action: Keep natural plant cordage and conceptual knots, lashings strictly non-life-safety (Z08-P44, Z09-P12..P21)—NEVER assign unvalidated breaking-strength pounds or use field knots for climbing, towing, or human suspension. @A04,R18,K04,K06
failure: Swinging a cracked-handle axe, cutting under-tension spring poles, or loading improvised cordage causes catastrophic lacerations, recoil trauma, and load drops. @K06,K09,K10
verify: Tool edges, handles pass daylight inspection, cutting circles are clear, and load-rating boundaries remain strictly observed. @K06,K08,K09
stop: Stop tool work immediately when fatigue, cold-numb fingers, loose heads, pinched saw kerfs, or tensioned timber appear. @K08,K09,K10
reviewer: Forestry sawyer, rigging, and tool-safety reviewer

Z16-P34 | Navigation, Map, Compass, Datum, PLB and Radio Equipment Index | New manuscript (Z16 P20 equipment index)
