action: Match map datum (WGS84 vs NAD27) to GPS settings before plotting coordinates (Z11-P12) and apply current local magnetic declination carefully—never inferring present-day declination from historical reference maps like the 1965 Ely excerpt (Z11-P14). @A01,N02,N03
action: Cross-check compass bearings against terrain features in northern Minnesota iron-formation and gabbro bedrock zones where magnetite deflects needles locally (Z08-P20, Z11-P29), and reject moss-on-north folklore unconditionally (Z11-P35). @A04,R20,N03
action: Keep paper maps and baseplate compass as primary cold-proof navigation alongside warm-carried electronics, and register 406 MHz PLBs, satellite messengers with NOAA before trips so rescue dispatch receives emergency contacts immediately (Z11-P56, Z11-P57). @A09,N08,N09
failure: Mixing NAD27 and WGS84 coordinates, ignoring iron-rock compass anomalies, or carrying an unregistered beacon delays SAR teams by miles or hours. @N02,N03,N08,R20
verify: Map vintage, datum, current declination, iron-rock cross-checks, and active beacon registration are verified pre-trip. @N02,N03,N08
stop: Stop advancing when position uncertainty grows; apply STOP (Z11-P43), relocate to known handrail, last verified point, or activate rescue signaling. @N01,N08
reviewer: Cartography, navigation, and SAR communications reviewer

Z16-P35 | Household Outage Power, Battery, Transfer Switch and Alert Gear Index | New manuscript (Z16 P20 equipment index)
objective: Synthesize safe portable-power, generator transfer-switch, lithium-battery thermal-runaway, and NOAA weather-radio equipment rules from Z13 and Z15.
applies: Residential power-outage readiness and severe-weather alerting.
equipment: Full offline reader (Z13, Z15), primary zone cards, and local emergency and agency references.
diagram: Locate Z13, Z15 cards | Preserve exact stop & limits | Defer to full zone card
visual: Cross-zone atlas schematic linking Z13, Z15 with preserved upstream conditions and stop thresholds.
action: Power household circuits from a portable generator ONLY through a licensed-electrician-installed transfer switch or approved interlock kit—NEVER backfeed a generator into a wall or dryer outlet (Z13-P07), keeping the unit at least 20 ft outdoors (Z13-P06). @A01,U04,C06
action: Inspect portable lithium-ion power stations for swelling, overheating, or flood submersion, storing and charging away from exits and combustibles (Z13-P11..P13); ventilate flooded lead-acid charging areas for hydrogen gas. @A01,U04
action: Keep a battery, hand-crank NOAA Weather Radio with SAME county alerts, battery-backed CO, smoke alarms on every level, and dry flashlights (avoiding open candles) ready for multi-day outages (Z13-P20, Z15-P02). @A09,U05,D01
failure: Backfeeding household wiring electrocutes utility linemen, while charging damaged lithium packs or burning unattended candles ignites structure fires. @U04,U05
verify: Transfer switch, heavy outdoor GFCI cord, intact battery packs, tested CO alarms, and NOAA radio readiness are confirmed. @U04,U05,D01
stop: Stop using any generator within 20 ft of openings, any swollen, wet lithium pack, or any wet electrical panel after flooding. @U04,U20
reviewer: Licensed master electrician and fire-safety reviewer

Z16-P36 | Home Food Preservation Equipment: Canners, Gauges and Thermometers Index | New manuscript (Z16 P20 equipment index)
objective: Cross-index USDA, NCHFP boiling-water, atmospheric-steam, and pressure-canner equipment rules alongside calibrated food thermometers from Z14 and Z06.
applies: Safe home canning, jerky dehydration, and wild-game, fish temperature verification.
equipment: Full offline reader (Z14, Z06), primary zone cards, and local emergency and agency references.
diagram: Locate Z14, Z06 cards | Preserve exact stop & limits | Defer to full zone card
visual: Cross-zone atlas schematic linking Z14, Z06 with preserved upstream conditions and stop thresholds.
action: Use a dedicated USDA-recommended pressure canner (holding at least 4 quart jars) for ALL low-acid foods (vegetables, meats, poultry, fish, soups), venting steady steam for 10 full minutes before pressurizing and testing dial gauges annually (Z14-P52..P56). @A03,P13,P14
action: Restrict boiling-water canners and research-tested atmospheric steam canners (at or below 45 min total including elevation) strictly to high-acid or properly acidified tested recipes—NEVER use electric multi-cookers, oven canning, or open-kettle canning (Z14-P48, P25). @A03,P11,P25
action: Use a calibrated digital probe thermometer to verify jerky pre-heating (160 F meat and 165 F poultry, Z14-P68, P24), wild-bear, omnivore cooking (at least 165 F, Z06-P40), freshwater fish (145 F, Z06-P42), and refrigerator cold-chain (at or below 40 F, Z14-P38). @A03,P24,H10,F01
failure: Skipping the 10-minute pressure-canner vent, trusting an uncalibrated dial gauge, or canning low-acid beans in a boiling-water bath creates lethal botulism conditions. @P13,P14,P23
verify: Tested equipment class, annual dial-gauge check, 10-minute steam vent, and calibrated probe thermometer are confirmed. @P13,P14,P24
stop: Stop processing if pressure drops below target mid-cycle (reprocess full time per NCHFP) or if unverified appliances are proposed. @P13,P14
reviewer: Food-preservation process authority and Extension reviewer

