action: Apply ordered non-destructive screening—daylight luster, cleavage-plane angle tilt, Mohs fingernail, copper, steel scratch steps, and porcelain streak—rather than unreliable bulk color (Z08-P02, Z08-P16, Z08-P17). @A04,R04
action: Distinguish hard conchoidal-fracturing silica rocks (chert, flint, jasper, quartz, Mohs ~7) from softer carbonates (calcite, dolostone) and blocky feldspars, micas while enforcing eye and silica-dust boundaries (Z08-P03, Z08-P15, Z08-P18, Z08-P19). @A04,R04,R05,R06
action: Keep wet, river-sourced, porous sandstone, shale, and unverified cobbles completely out of campfires and boiling setups due to violent steam spalling (Z08-P22, Z03-P01). @A04,R13
failure: Heating creek cobbles, breaking fibrous metamorphic veins, or dry-chipping quartz without PPE causes eye trauma, spalling injuries, and silica exposure. @R06,R07,R13
verify: Non-destructive checks, silica, asbestos exclusions, and zero unverified fire-stone use stay enforced. @R04,R06,R13
stop: Stop handling immediately if fibrous veins, bright heavy metallic crusts, or visible mineral dust appear. @R06,R07,R14
reviewer: Mineralogist and industrial hygienist

Z16-P39 | Wood Species, Grain Runout and B007, B008 Historical Lineage Index | New manuscript (Z16 P20 material index)
objective: Cross-reference dead-downed wood moisture, grain screening, tree identification, and reconciled B007, B007A, B008, B011 material holds across four zones.
