action: Screen dead downed wood for dryness, straight continuous grain, non-punky firmness, and absence of fungal conks or overhead widowmaker snags (Z08-P33..P35, Z08-P40, Z09-P48). @A04,R15,K09
action: Preserve reconciled B007, B008 friction-material distinctions: dry low-resin basswood, aspen, cedar, cottonwood, and mullein for controlled training versus pitchy resinous fatwood strictly for lawful outdoor tinder—never relying on friction fire in hypothermic emergencies (Z08-P41..P45, Z03-P12). @A04,R15,C04,C16
action: Respect public-land tree protection and firewood pest quarantines (emerald ash borer): never cut live trees, never peel live birch, cedar, elm bark, and cross-check Z05 tree taxonomy, photo holds (Z08-P34, Z08-P36, Z05-P44..P53). @A04,A05,R09,R15,B16
