action: Never infer structural load capacities in pounds, kilograms, or kilonewtons for wild wood spans, shelter roofs, snow trenches, rock anchors, or hand-twisted cordage (Z02-P33, Z08-P52, Z09-P45). @A04,E16,R15,K06
action: Never infer food-contact or drinking-water chemical safety from visual cleanliness of stones, wild clay, galvanized, painted scrap, or driftwood (Z08-P53, Z04-P01). @A04,R12,R14
action: Use manufacturer-rated, inspected commercial hardware and food-grade tested vessels whenever human life safety, overhead loads, or food, water heating are involved. @A04,K06,W11
failure: Treating a visual field guide as an engineering specification or food-safety lab test causes structural collapse or heavy-metal poisoning. @E16,R14,K06
verify: Non-certification disclaimers stay visible across every shelter, tool, rigging, and material reference. @R15,K06
stop: Stop any plan relying on unverified wild materials for climbing, hoisting, overhead shelter loads, or cookware. @R14,R15,K06
reviewer: Structural engineer, materials scientist, and toxicologist

