action: When position is lost, execute STOP immediately (Sit, Think, Observe, Plan, Z11-P43), stay put near clear visibility, shelter rather than wandering off search grids, and deploy three-blast whistle, mirror, high-contrast ground signals plus registered PLB, SOS if needed (Z11-P53..P58). @A01,A09,N07,N08
action: Maintain strict helicopter landing-zone exclusion and follow ONLY rescue-crew hand, voice directions—never approaching an aircraft from an assumed universal safe quadrant (Z11-P65). @A01,N09
failure: Continuing to walk blindly after losing position or rushing toward a landing rescue helicopter causes search delays and fatal rotor trauma. @N07,N09
verify: Continuous map-terrain tracking, STOP hold, three-signal convention, and crew-directed aviation boundaries stay intact. @N01,N07,N09
