action: Enforce layperson scope strictly (Z10-P01): zero unauthorized medication mg, mL dosing, zero invasive procedures (tracheotomy, cutting wounds, bites, suturing), and prompt 911, dispatcher activation for red flags. @A03,M01,M22
action: Clean minor wounds with safe potable water and clean dressings (Z10-P20), cool thermal burns with cool running water (no ice, butter, Z10-P26), pad extremity splints across adjacent joints while checking distal circulation, sensation, motion (CSM, Z10-P32), and follow CDC seizure timing (>5 min = 911, Z10-P53, M29) and awake-only fast sugar for known hypoglycemia (Z10-P54, M30). @A03,M06,M08,M29,M30
action: Record timed vital trends, allergies, medications, and interventions (SAMPLE, AVPU notes, Z10-P70) to hand directly to EMS or hospital clinicians. @A03,M22
failure: Giving oral sugar to an unconscious diabetic, restraining a seizing patient, or skipping distal CSM checks after splinting causes aspiration or limb ischemia. @M08,M29,M30
verify: Layperson boundaries, CSM splinting checks, seizure, hypoglycemia triggers, and written patient logs remain preserved. @M06,M29,M30
stop: Stop lay field management and evacuate or call 911 immediately for worsening alertness, airway compromise, uncontrolled bleeding, or loss of distal pulse, sensation. @M01,M08
reviewer: Wilderness-medicine physician and EMS director

Z16-P46 | Food Cold-Chain, Safe Cooking Temperatures and Outage Spoilage Index | New manuscript (Z16 P20 food safety index)
objective: Harmonize refrigerator, freezer outage timelines, wild-game, fish cooking temperatures, and Clean, Separate, Cook, Chill hygiene across Z14, Z06, and Z13.
applies: Power outages, field-game processing, and everyday food-spoilage triage.
equipment: Full offline reader (Z14, Z06, Z13), primary zone cards, and local emergency and agency references.
diagram: Locate Z14, Z06, Z13 cards | Preserve exact stop & limits | Defer to full zone card
visual: Cross-zone atlas schematic linking Z14, Z06, Z13 with preserved upstream conditions and stop thresholds.
action: Keep refrigerator doors closed during outages (cold holds roughly 4 hours; full closed freezer ~48 hours, half-full ~24 hours) and verify at or below 40 F with an appliance thermometer—discarding perishable foods held above 40 F over 2 hours (1 hour if > 90 F) per Z14-P38..P41. @A03,F01,P09
action: Verify internal cooking temperatures strictly with a calibrated food thermometer rather than color: freshwater fish 145 F (Z06-P42), whole-muscle jerky wet-heat 160 F meat and 165 F poultry (Z14-P68, P24), and wild bear, omnivore game at least 165 F for freeze-resistant Trichinella (Z06-P40). @A03,F02,H10,P24
action: Never taste questionable outage or wild-game meat to test safety—pathogenic bacteria and toxins frequently show zero off-odor (Z14-P41, Z06-P43). @A03,F01,H17
failure: Tasting warm outage leftovers, refreezing completely thawed warm meat, or relying on freezing to kill bear Trichinella causes severe foodborne illness. @F01,H10
verify: Thermometer verification, 4-hour fridge and 40 F thresholds, and zero taste-testing rules stay aligned across zones. @F01,F02,H10
stop: Stop and discard any perishable food exceeding safe time-temperature limits or lacking thermometer verification. @F01
reviewer: Food-safety microbiologist and Extension reviewer

