action: Route foods strictly by pH and tested USDA, NCHFP recipe: low-acid foods (pH > 4.6: vegetables, meats, poultry, fish, beans, soups) MUST be pressure-canned—NEVER water-bath, oven, open-kettle, or multi-cooker canned (Z14-P45..P56). @A03,P11,P13
action: Follow exact tomato acidification (citric acid or bottled lemon juice even when pressure-canning per NCHFP, P22), reject tomatoes from frost-killed, dead vines, and adjust boiling time or pressure PSI for elevations above 1,000 feet (Z14-P49, Z14-P55). @A03,P12,P22
action: Inspect cooled two-piece lids without screw bands (Z14-P59) and treat bulging, leaking, spurting, or suspicious jars under NCHFP botulism detoxification, disposal without tasting—calling 911 immediately for any neurologic botulism signs (Z14-P61, Z14-P62, P23). @A03,P15,P23
failure: Omitting tomato acidification, skipping altitude PSI boosts, or altering salsa, vegetable ratios creates fatal Clostridium botulinum toxin risk. @P11,P13,P22,P23
verify: Tested USDA, NCHFP recipe, exact acid, altitude adjustment, 10-minute steam vent, and zero-taste spoilage rules remain intact. @P11,P13,P22
stop: Stop canning immediately if an untested family recipe, uncalibrated dial gauge, or oven, open-kettle shortcut is suggested. @P11,P13
