action: Define core A–B terms consistently: Acidification (adding measured bottled lemon juice or citric acid per NCHFP to lower tomato pH at or below 4.6, Z14); Amatoxin (heat-stable lethal hepatotoxin in Amanita, Galerina, Z05); Annulus (stem ring remnant of partial veil, Z05); Backfeeding (illegal lethal generator-to-outlet connection, Z13). @A07,P22,B06,U04
action: Define core C terms consistently: Candled ice (deteriorating vertical-column spring ice, Z12); Cicutoxin (lethal convulsant in water hemlock, Z05); Cleavage vs Conchoidal fracture (atomic planar split vs curved glassy silica break, Z08); Cortina (cobweb veil in Cortinarius, Z05). @A07,X03,B11,R04
action: Define clinical, wildlife C terms: CSM check (distal circulation, sensation, motion after splinting, Z10); CWD (Chronic Wasting Disease fatal cervid prion illness not destroyed by cooking, Z06); Cyanotoxin (algal toxin concentrated by boiling HAB water, Z04). @A07,M08,H09,W04
failure: Inconsistent definitions across chapters blur safety boundaries such as acidification, candled ice, or cleavage versus fracture. @A07
verify: Every glossary term cites its governing upstream zone and adds zero ungrounded operational instructions. @A07
stop: Stop using glossary definitions as standalone instructions; open the cited zone card for full conditions and stop rules. @A07,A10
reviewer: Multi-domain technical editor

